<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>More people work from home, more families are staying put instead of moving, and everyone's short on space. A garden room answers all three: a home office, a gym, a studio or an extra room at the bottom of the garden, without the upheaval of an extension. Demand is high. The job is getting seen by the homeowners who want one before your competitor does.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Garden offices and studios</li>
        <li>Home gyms and hobby rooms</li>
        <li>Garden bars and entertaining spaces</li>
        <li>Extra living space and annexes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why real footage wins</h2>
      <p>A garden room sells on the finish. A homeowner needs to picture a proper insulated, finished room in their own garden, not a shed. Real footage of your builds, filmed on site or from finished jobs, never stock, is what makes that click. Seeing the quality inside and out is exactly what turns a scroller into a serious enquiry.</p>

      <h2>What the funnel asks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>What's it for, an office, gym, studio or extra room?</li>
        <li>Roughly what size, and how's the garden accessed?</li>
        <li>What type of property, and the postcode?</li>
        <li>When are they looking to get it done, and the best number to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That sorts the homeowners serious about adding space from the ones just browsing ideas, so you're quoting real builds.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
    </div>

